BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20230422
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20230423
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:0ACA2C9F-1C43-4941-A64B-4EDE9CCD2CA9
CREATED:20230419T192941Z
DESCRIPTION:The World's Easiest and Most Egg-cellent Way to Show up for UUP
 ... Butter and Eggs Day Parade on Saturday\, April 22th.\nWe have been invi
 ted by our friends from El Dia de los Muertos Petaluma and Petaluma Paquiyo
 llotzin (Joyful Heart in the Aztec language) to join with them as one joyfu
 lly united entry in the upcoming Butter and Eggs Day Parade.  All you have 
 to do is bring your best smile\, wear a UUP t-shirt if you have one\, and s
 how up!  We'll have a few signs to hold\, a banner to carry and our mission
  statement in Spanish and English to pass out.  The more of us\, the merrie
 r our parade party! Check out the UUP email next Wednesday for our staging 
 area and time to gather. If you have any questions\, please contact Jodi Bo
 yle.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230422T073543Z
LOCATION:Downtown Petaluma
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Butter & Eggs Day Parade
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20070311T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20070311T113000
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:2bcetof22gmlselq3m2c3sa0pc@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20070311T103000
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20070301T051255Z
DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\n“In Praise of Sweet Darkness”
  titles Shepherd Bliss’ guest presentation March 11. He will be accompanied
  throughout the talk by musicians from the Kokopelli Players\, including aw
 ard-winning art teacher and CD recording artist Larry Stefl on guitar and a
 n indigenous flute called the huaca and by Peter Herbert of the UU Congrega
 tion in Marin on drums and other percussion.\n\nShepherd will focus on the 
 benevolent aspects of darkness\, such as chocolate. Rumi\, Lao Tzu\, Unitar
 ian Ralph Waldo Emerson\, Wendell Berry\, David Whyte\, Rilke and T.S. Elio
 t will be among the poets quoted. Mystics quoted will include St. Francis o
 f Assisi\, St. Thomas of Aquinas\, Meister Eckhard\, and St. John of the Cr
 oss’ classic “Dark Night of the Soul.” Psychologist Carl Jung’s concept of 
 the shadow will also be employed. Shepherd will refer to his work at Kokope
 lli Farm south of Sebastopol.\n\nShepherd is currently writing a book on th
 is subject. He welcomes stories of people’s personal experiences with darkn
 ess and references to other sources\, which can be sent to sb3@pon.net.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
