BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160117T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160117T123000
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:0v3e555b2rfof21p4gnok2det4@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20160117T113000
CREATED:20151001T192018Z
DESCRIPTION:Empathy is a Verb\n\nJavier Antezana\, Speaker\; Ellen Beeler\,
  Worship Associate\;  Jesus Contreras\, Music Director\; Jim Lewis\, Direct
 or of Religious Education\n\nAs we continue our January theme\, “Trailblaze
 rs for Justice\,” we learn about Javier Antezana and his personal story in 
 working as an advocate in the most heartbreaking situations and among the m
 ost vulnerable people\, some of whom who could be quite intimidating.\n\nAs
  a case manager for San Francisco’s General Hospital’s violence-interventio
 n program\, the Wraparound Project\, Javier was one of the first people to 
 approach a patient’s bedside when doctors rushed a gunshot victim to the Em
 ergency Room. Years later\, life changed for Javier when he had a family an
 d m0ved to Sonoma County to become Community Organizer with the Petaluma Da
 y Labor Initiative.
LAST-MODIFIED:20211110T145004Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Worship
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
