BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20130518T160000Z
DTEND:20130518T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:lksv4j176vkm0r7v25ids4ecr4@google.com
CREATED:20130425T115306Z
DESCRIPTION:Safe Congregations Workshop May 18th\nJenn Gray and Jim Lewis\,
  Workshop Leaders\nThis is an interactive workshop for Religious Educators\
 , volunteers\, congregational leaders\, and members. We will explore togeth
 er the UUA’s Safe Congregations guidelines\, with a focus on children and y
 outh. From the UUA website (http://www.uua.org/safe/index.shtml) “Although 
 no policy or knowledge of the issues can absolutely guarantee safety in you
 r congregation under all circumstances\, congregations can take pro-active 
 steps to create environments that are safe and prepared.” The majority of t
 he day will focus on Safe Congregations material. A small portion of the da
 y will also cover suicide prevention techniques. \n\nJenn Gray\, has previo
 usly trained educators on mandated reporting. She also worked for the State
  of Kansas\, for five years\, in the department of Social and Rehabilitatio
 n Services Protection Report Center. Two years ago\, she became a certified
  trainer in a suicide prevention technique called “Question\, Persuade\, Re
 fer”.\nThis workshop will be held at the Unitarian Universalist Congregatio
 n of Marin on Saturday\, May 18th from 9am – 3pm. Please register at:\nhttp
 s://docs.google.com/forms/d/1gZTYo0xmnwap6wQyB3vIND7A7fa71Mj8lhMUptriR0s/vi
 ewform If you have questions please contact Jenn Gray at Jenn.Leota.Gray@gm
 ail.com  \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034721Z
LOCATION:United Universalist Congregation in Marin
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Safe Congregations Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
