CREATED:20070301T051255Z
DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\n"Realism and Hope"\nGuest Spe
 aker: Earl Cruser\nAs we look at many trends in our communities and world t
 oday\, there are many reasons to be pessimistic about the future. Are there
  reasons to hope for a better world for future generations? Without belief 
 in an omnipotent god\, is there any reason to hope? Kurt Vonnegut\, Michael
  Lerner\, Barak Obama and Victor Frankl will be peeked out to see where we 
 might look. This is also an introduction to Rabbi Lerner's book: "The Left 
 Hand of God" that we hope to use in an adult RE group in June\, July and Au
 gust. \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
