UID:0s2ifhvhncnb3cdmu0kvk0feuo@google.com
CREATED:20131012T144826Z
DESCRIPTION:The North Bay Organizing Project cordially invites the public t
 o attend our 2013 Public Meeting at the Sonoma Academy\, 2500 Farmers Lane\
 , Santa Rosa\, Ca (end of Kawana Springs Road off of Petaluma Hill Road).\n
 \nAs members of NBOP UUP helps build community power by uniting people of s
 hared values to act together\, and the Public Meeting is the public express
 ion of this. The Public Meeting is the space that we intentionally create s
 o that ordinary people can have a voice in our democracy\, come experience 
 what it feels like. We have worked with endless energy and love\, and we kn
 ow that organized people can win! We need all of our members and allies pre
 sent to assure commitments from public officials on the issues that are clo
 se to our hearts.\n- Our Immigration Task Force will culminate their work t
 o minimize deportations in Sonoma County\, as well as to support the passag
 e of just comprehensive immigration reform.\n- Our Education Task Force wil
 l also culminate their work to ensure a new Restorative Discipline policy t
 hat would minimize suspensions and expulsions in the Santa Rosa City School
 s\, and end Zero Tolerance school discipline policies.\n- Our Transportatio
 n/ Neighborhood Development Task Force will also announce the formation of 
 a Transit Riders Union that will further the struggle for better public tra
 nsportation services.\nFor more information email Ruth at lorain.ruth@gmail
 .com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034705Z
LOCATION:Sonoma Academy\, 2500 Farmers Lane\, Santa Rosa\, Ca
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The North Bay Organizing Project 2013 Public Meeting
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
