DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\nThe People With Eyes on Our F
 eet\nGuest Speaker: Rev. Denis Letourneau Paul\, Faithful Fools Street Mini
 stry\, SF\nWorship Leader: Joyce Tischler\nWild animals have an amazing cap
 acity to heal themselves to prevent stress.  Humans go to therapists to ove
 rcome the wounds we experience in our family systems and out in the world. 
  But what about the really big injuries\, the injuries that plague the worl
 d family and the global body?  How can we learn from the animals and our fa
 milies to live out the call of Unitarian Universalism and be a force of hea
 ling and compassion?  The answer may well be in our feet.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
