UID:dd5h4mbuuesdgmep5njtoaals8@google.com
CREATED:20130419T151517Z
DESCRIPTION:UUP is sponsoring two special Earth Day events that will take p
 lace at Aqus Cafe\, 189 H Street. Sunday\, April 21 at 7pm. BIDDER 70\, 72 
 minute film. BIDDER 70 follows Tim DeChristopher\, a University of Utah stu
 dent\, who on December 19\, 2008\,in a dazzling act of civil disobedience\,
  derailed the outgoing Bush administration’s illegal Bureau of Land Managem
 ent oil and gas auction. As bidder #70\, Tim bid 1.8 million dollars and wo
 n 22\,000 pristine acres surrounding Utah’s National Parks. He had no inten
 tion to pay or drill. In February 2009\, the new Obama administration agree
 d the land should be safeguarded and invalidated the entire auction.  Never
 theless\, Tim was indicted on two federal felonies with penalties of up to 
 ten years in prison. Tim will be released from his two years in prison on\,
  April 21st\, the very day we will be seeing the film at Aqus. In September
 \, Tim will be attending Harvard Divinity School on a full scholarship to b
 ecome a UU minister.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034509Z
LOCATION:AQUS Cafe\, 2nd and H Streets\, Petaluma
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:BIDDER 70 Screening
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
