BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20160222T013000Z
DTEND:20160222T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:3kv5aov6sai0ieudbpam378qbc@google.com
CREATED:20160126T220250Z
DESCRIPTION:I'm glad we're going to accept our Muslim neighbors' invitation
  to join them for a potluck and service. They are very excited about the op
 portunity to have us with them.\n\nIn addition\, there will be some people 
 coming from my neighborhood (the extended neighborhood reached by Next Door
 )--probably 5-7 people. Reverend Blythe of United Church of Christ was also
  at the original meeting at Aqus\, and I imagine she and perhaps some membe
 rs of UCC may be there.\n\nAgain\, we gather at the mosque on Sunday\, Febr
 uary 7\, 5:30--at the Islamic Center at 222 Bassett\, Petaluma.\n\nI've att
 ached as a document the one-page hand-out I gave you on Sunday\, and most o
 f the details are there. Mary\, I think you know all the details already\; 
 and George\, Ellen put your name down and has the information to share.\n\n
 In addition to the information on the hand-out\, I mentioned a few other th
 ings when most of us talked after the service on Sunday:\n--take shoes off 
 at door\n--no alcohol\, including no alcohol in dishes brought to share at 
 the potluck\n--most Muslim women don't shake hands with a man not in her fa
 mily\; most Muslim men don't shake hands with women not in their family\n--
 Muslims aren't necessarily vegetarians\, but have asked that we bring fruit
 s/veggies/vegetarian food because halal meat isn't that easy to find. So so
 me of them may bring meat dishes.\n--there will be a speaker after their pr
 ayers and before the potluck who will talk with us about Islam\, thinking t
 hat we might want a brief overview. The Imam is shy because of his English\
 , so they are getting another speaker.\n\nBrief background:\nOne of my neig
 hbors wondered on Next Door (neighborhood list serv) "how we can be good ne
 ighbors to our Muslim community members in trying times." (The trying times
  included the kind of things being said by a number of presidential candida
 tes and their followers\, as well as other slurs.)\n\nOut of that came an i
 nformal meeting at Aqus. Four Muslim neighbors  (2 women\, 2 men) came to t
 he meeting. They said several times how very touched they were by this desi
 re to help.\n\nThe four said they were not experiencing negative things in 
 Petaluma (except for graffiti painted on the mosque every week\, which they
  thought was done by high school students--they kind of minimized this and 
 said they just painted it over each week--I hope this can be stopped\, thou
 gh).\n\nAgain\, the one thing they did want was to have more connection wit
 h the non-Muslim community. So their invitation to us came soon after that.
 \n\nAny further questions\, or desires to go together\, or anything else\, 
 just call or email me.\n\nOh\, one other thing: our group was contacted by 
 the Sonoma County Muslim Outreach Group. They are heading up a similar outr
 each across the county\, and have invited any of us to attend their late Ja
 nuary meeting. Will send more info about that in case anyone is interested.
 \n\nI'm looking forward to this!
LAST-MODIFIED:20160126T220635Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: Muslim Mosque in  Petaluma Visit
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
