DTEND:20130421T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:pjrv7cjooapgoskklsvnqt03vc@google.com
CREATED:20130419T151358Z
DESCRIPTION:LIVING ROOM CHAT on the PETALUMA VILLAGE EXPLORATION PROJECT\nS
 unday April 21\, 2 - 3:30 PM\nInformal presentation by Anne Greenblatt and 
 Camille Jordan on the Village model\, with lots of discussion on how partic
 ipants might see a Village working in Petaluma\, and our progress so far in
  exploring the idea for our community.  Villages are non-profit\, membershi
 p organizations to enable adults 50+ to live active\, vibrant\, & connected
  lives in our own homes as we age. Think neighbors helping neighbors\, shar
 ing\, support in navigating systems\, & peace of mind.\n\nMembers call one 
 number for resource referral\, home visits and check-ins\, medical advocacy
 \, minor household repairs\, social events\, transportation\, and opportuni
 ties to share one's special talents within the Village and larger community
 . Your ideas are needed as we explore this innovative model for our town! H
 eld at home of Camille Jordan\, 110 Glendon Way (off Mt. View). \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034458Z
LOCATION:110 Glendon Way\, Petaluma
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Petaluma Village Exploration Project
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
