DESCRIPTION:UUP Social Justice\n Saturday April 2 from 10:00 a.m. to 2:00 p
 .m. \nPlanning Meeting:   Exploring a voter engagement effort for Petaluma 
 \n\n...NBOP\, St Vincent\, St. John’s Episcopal\, jointly with George Beele
 r representing UUP are exploring a voter engagement effort for Petaluma. We
  are in the beginning stages of planning. We may only target a couple of pr
 ecincts with a history of low voter turnout and high percentage of renters.
  Yesterday Margie Helm hosted a meeting with Davin\, Teresa Lopez\, Abraham
  Solar\, Rev. Daniel\, Annie Dobbs-Kramer\, and me. We hope to have other c
 ivic groups involved. Petaluma Tomorrow representatives were not able to at
 tend but are very interested in participating. UCC are also invited to part
 icipate\n\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160314T185522Z
LOCATION: 825 Middlefield Rd\, Petaluma\, (Fellowship hall )
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:UUP Social Justice NBOP Exploring a voter engagement effort for Pet
 aluma
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
