DTEND:20160212T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:i46joi8cnsshngffv4k88tleks@google.com
CREATED:20160109T023843Z
DESCRIPTION:Contact Carol West (707) 481-7965 carolfayewest@gmail.com\n\nW3
 003 Untangling the Triangles\nwith Rev. Carol McKinley\, PNWD Healthy Congr
 egations Team\nThursday | February 11\, 2016 | 6:30-7:30 pm PT \nWhat are “
 triangulated conversations” anyway\, and what’s the big deal about them? Tr
 iangulated conversations happen when an issue arises and you find yourself 
 and others talking about someone\, rather than to someone. In congregations
 \, we can quickly get caught up in tangles of triangles when we’re trying t
 o help – or when someone else wants us to take care of something messy they
  don’t want to deal with. When a sympathetic ear becomes a funnel for gossi
 p\, when you feel manipulated and used\, when suddenly it’syour problem\, c
 hances are you’ve been triangulated. This webinar will help you identify tr
 iangles and straighten out lines of communication to take you out of the mi
 ddle
LAST-MODIFIED:20160109T023900Z
LOCATION:64 Century Ln\, Petaluma\, CA 94952\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:W3003 Untangling the Triangles
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
