CREATED:20160812T174108Z
DESCRIPTION:Interdependence Day - November 12\nBuilding Beloved Community -
  Saturday\, November 12. Registration opens at 9:00AM\; our program runs fr
 om 9:30AM – 4:30PM. Hosted by the UU Congregation in Santa Rosa\, $10 cover
 s refreshments and materials. Lunch will be on your own. We will encourage 
 people who are attending to join together and meet someone new.\n\nClergy a
 nd Lay Leaders are invited to a day of deep connection\, celebration and le
 arning. Our day will begin with a worship service with a full band and end 
 with a blessing of the leaders.\nThe learning will include:\n\nOur Covenant
 al Faith and Beloved Community: Exploring the Connections\n \nHelping Thing
 s Go Right in Your Congregation\nAn ounce of prevention is still worth a po
 und of cure\, or maybe even more. Much of the conflict in congregations can
  be avoided by paying attention to these basic things.\n\nPaths to Healing\
 nNo matter what steps we take\, conflict is inevitable. When responded to i
 n healthy ways\, it can be used to create and strengthen relationships and 
 our congregations and help us serve as a beacon to the world.\n\nRegistrati
 on will open soon.   (back to top)  \n 
LAST-MODIFIED:20160812T174108Z
LOCATION:Glaser Center\, 547 Mendocino Ave\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95401\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:UUA Interdependence Day 
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
