UID:qa7p22lq0gdhhgu0sl3h88lnps@google.com
CREATED:20080822T130357Z
DESCRIPTION:Marriage Rights Attorney to Speak at the Unitarian Universalist
 s of Petaluma\n\nTherese Stewart\, Chief Deputy City Attorney for the City 
 and County of San \nFrancisco\, who argued the case for same sex marriage r
 ights before the California Supreme Court\, will speak twice on Sunday\, Se
 ptember 14 at the Unitarian Universalists of Petaluma (UUP)—first\, in the 
 regular worship service at 10:30 a.m.\, and then in an afternoon presentati
 on from 1 to 3 p.m. Both events are open to the public.\nStewart is the dau
 ghter of UUP member Hope Stewart.\nStewart’s afternoon talk\, entitled “The
  California Supreme Court Decision Legalizing Gay Marriage: The Inside Stor
 y” will feature a personal description of what it was like to argue such an
  important case\, followed by a question and answer opportunity. A $5 donat
 ion is requested.\nStewart was the lead attorney representing the City in t
 he California Marriage Equality Cases.  She represented the City in challen
 ging the marriage laws' exclusion of same-sex couples under the State Const
 itution and argued the case before the California Supreme Court.\n“To have 
 the lead attorney on such an historic case come speak in Petaluma is a wond
 erful opportunity\,” said Jean Conrad\, UUP’s Board President. “We feel pro
 ud and privileged to host Terry.”\nThe Unitarian Universalist Association h
 as consistently stood for marriage equality\, frequently using the phrase c
 oined by Association President\, Rev. William Sinkford\, that they “stand o
 n the side of love.” \nBoth events will be held at the Petaluma Woman’s Clu
 b\, the regular meeting place of UUP\, at 518 B St.\, Petaluma. For more in
 formation\, or directions\, visit www.uupetaluma.org.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034728Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, CA 94952
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:“The California Supreme Court Decision Legalizing Gay Marriage: The
  Inside Story”
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
