CREATED:20070301T051255Z
DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\nWisdom Born of Compassion\nSp
 eaker: Daniel Potter\nWorship Leaders: Ellen Beeler and Stacey Meinzen\nGue
 st speaker Daniel Potter from the Mahakaruna Meditation Center blesses us w
 ith his return. We often feel pain at the heart when we observe someone suf
 fering. And this feeling can spur us to take action\, especially if the per
 son suffering is someone we love. But if we leave this process unexamined w
 e may discover over time that we are unconsciously perpetuating the very pr
 ocess we are hoping to change\, or least affect\, in some positive way. Thi
 s is why we need wisdom. Eventually we will find that wisdom born of compas
 sion is our most precious possession and forms the basis of true love.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
