BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20071111T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20071111T113000
DTSTAMP:20260514T024000Z
UID:2bcetof22gmlselq3m2c3sa0pc@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20071111T103000
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20070301T051255Z
DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\n"Now is the Time! Celebrating
  Unitarian Universalism and Growing our Faith" Minister: Rev. Ben Kocs-Meye
 rs\nWorship Associate: Diana Spaulding.\nNo man is an island...and no congr
 egation stands alone. Our congregation is only one small strand of a larger
  interconnected web of Unitarian Universalist congregations. What does it m
 ean to us personally to be part of a larger faith movement? What does it me
 an to our congregation to be part of the UUA? Today we begin to strengthen 
 the bonds of our common purpose and combine our resources to make Unitarian
  Universalism a stronger voice for liberal religious values in our country.
  Please join in this service as we\, along with all UU congregations across
  the continent\, celebrate and support our Unitarian Universalist Associati
 on. All are welcome! 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
