DESCRIPTION:Ric Masten is the author of numerous books of poetry. He was or
 dained as a UU minister by virtue of his service in poetry to our movement\
 , and is the composer of "Let It Be A Dance\," in our hymnal. He'll be givi
 ng the message of the morning at UUP on July 1\, and the afternoon before\,
  on June 30\, he will present a very special afternoon of poetry in an inti
 mate setting--watch for details\, as we are still working out the exact tim
 e and place. But be sure and save the time for this opportunity to hear\, u
 p close\, a legend of Unitarian Universalism. For more about Ric\, see http
 ://www.ric-masten.net/AboutRicMasten.html.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034718Z
LOCATION:At the home of David Dodd and Diana Spaulding\, 716 Bassett St.\, 
 Petaluma\, CA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:An Afternoon with Ric Masten
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
