CREATED:20150930T175117Z
DESCRIPTION:This is a night for all ages to hear the story of the Nativity\
 , with some twists and turns along the way\, and to sing the old songs of C
 hristmas.  Our service will be from 4 to 5 pm\, with social time in the Fel
 lowship Hall from 3:30 to 4 and 5 to 5:30.  Larking About Choir will sing. 
  With Reverend Mary\, David Dodd\, Jesus Contreras\, Jim Lewis and cast of 
 children\, youth and adults presenting the Pageant.\n \nWe will accept with
  gratefulness contributions for the Unitarian Universalist Service Committe
 e\, Guest at Your Table program.  Please bring your boxes!\n \nIf you would
  like to contribute a savory or sweet to our social time please bring by 3:
 30 to the Fellowship Hall.  Please connect with Ruth Lorain lorain.ruth@gma
 il.com if you would like to help with simple set up or group clean up.\n 
LAST-MODIFIED:20151216T205632Z
LOCATION:Sanctuary and Fellowship Hall
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Christmas Eve Service & Social Time
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
