CREATED:20070301T051255Z
DESCRIPTION:Weekly worship service begins at 10:30 a.m. Coffee\, tea\, bage
 ls at 10 a.m. and also after the service. \n\nMarch 25: ONE WOMAN'S HISTORY
 \n------------------\nDuring Women's History Month\, it's only natural to r
 eflect on the changes that women have made in their lives over the past 50 
 years. It's not only the history we read about in books and moments in grea
 t movements that we think about\, it's also about how these events have sha
 ped women's lives. And\, our personal histories as 21st century\nwomen\, is
  a great place to start.\n\nMaxine Levaren is a writer\, personal success c
 oach\, relative newcomer to UU and a lifelong feminist.  Although she hates
  to admit it\, she remembers the 60s well\, looks back on it with nostalgia
 \, and views herself as an unrepentant hippie.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T034632Z
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman's Club\, 518 B St.\, Petaluma\, California
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sunday Worship
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
